  "wilson_floor_rule": "A judge category's 95% Wilson lower bound must be at least (n / (n + 1.96^2)) - judge_wilson_slack, i.e. statistically indistinguishable from all-pass at 95%. Defining the floor as a function of n rather than as a fixed constant is what keeps it meaningful as pending cases activate: at n=4 an all-pass bound is 0.510 and at n=10 it is 0.723, and a single fixed number cannot be right for both. The normal-approximation (Wald) interval is not used: it is unreliable below a few hundred datapoints."
